<h1>Jim Gardiner</h1>
<p>45th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Is seeking a third term, Nadig Newspapers reported in August 2026. He has pointed to about $500 million in redevelopment investment at Six Corners during his time in office and has said public safety is a top priority. No campaign website found.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>45th Ward alderman since 2019; Chicago firefighter on leave while serving; 45th Ward Democratic committeeperson from 2020 to 2024.</p>
